  "stories": 2,
  "description_text": "From the deck of this 1920 Madrona Craftsman, watch sailboats cross Lake Washington with the floating bridges and Bellevue skyline in the distance. The Cascades stretch across the horizon, and on clear days Mount Rainier comes into view. Tucked at the end of 38th Avenue, the house faces east, with lake views from decks on all three levels. Oak floors catch morning light in the living room. On rainy afternoons, settle in by the wood-burning fireplace and watch the clouds roll by. A wide opening leads to the formal dining room, with space for a long table and French doors that let the party spill onto the full-length deck. In the kitchen, cherry cabinetry and slab granite counters pair with stainless appliances, and heated floors make an early start a little easier. Upstairs, exposed beams follow the pitch of a wood-lined ceiling, with skylights overhead and lake views through the windows. The home's 2,440 finished square feet include bedrooms on the main and upper floors and a daylight lower level. A separate entrance, second kitchen, full bath and dedicated laundry give guests room to make breakfast, unwind after a day out and keep their own hours. A patio and detached one-car garage complete the property. Head up to 34th Avenue for brunch at Hi Spot Cafe and a browse through the shops, or follow a trail through Madrona Woods and spend the afternoon at Madrona Beach. Come home in time to pull up a chair on the deck as Bellevue's lights shimmer across the lake.",
